      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is about double the maximum labeled metformin dose. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nPlease check whether one of these was intended:\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg BID with meals\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO BID or TID with meals**, or another dose you had in mind\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Pharmacy will probably flag it either way."
      }
     ],
